---
import EnglishSiteLayout from "../../layouts/EnglishSiteLayout.astro";
---
<EnglishSiteLayout
  title="About Canapalandia | Independent hemp, CBD and cannabis journalism"
  description="Learn what Canapalandia is, what it covers and the editorial principles behind its reporting on hemp, CBD, cannabis and regulation."
  canonical="/en/about/"
  alternateIt="/chi-siamo/"
>
  <article class="en-page">
    <header>
      <p class="eyebrow">About us</p>
      <h1>Independent information on hemp, CBD, cannabis and policy.</h1>
      <p class="lead">Canapalandia is an independent editorial project focused on clear, sourced reporting and practical explainers for readers who want context rather than slogans.</p>
    </header>

    <section>
      <h2>What we cover</h2>
      <p>Our work spans industrial hemp, CBD, cannabis policy, medical cannabis, sustainability, research, markets and the cultural debate surrounding these subjects in Italy and Europe.</p>
      <p>English-language articles are selected and maintained as part of the same editorial archive, with explicit links to their Italian counterparts when a verified equivalent exists.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>How we work</h2>
      <p>We distinguish facts from interpretation, regulations from political claims and preliminary evidence from stronger scientific conclusions. When a topic is uncertain or changing, we state that uncertainty directly.</p>
      <p>Older material that no longer meets the current editorial standard can be placed under review and removed from indexing until its sources and wording are reassessed.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>What Canapalandia is not</h2>
      <p>Canapalandia is not a medical service, a legal-advice service or a substitute for professional advice. The editorial project does not present articles as individual therapeutic instructions.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Corrections and transparency</h2>
      <p>If you find an error, an outdated source or a passage that needs more context, you can contact the editorial team. Commercial collaborations and advertising are kept separate from editorial content and should be clearly identified.</p>
      <p><a href="/en/contact/">Contact the editorial team →</a></p>
    </section>
  </article>
</EnglishSiteLayout>
<style>
  .en-page{max-width:820px;margin:0 auto;padding:2.5rem 0 5rem}.eyebrow{color:var(--brand);font:700 .78rem/1.2 Archivo,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase}.en-page h1{margin:.35rem 0 1rem;font:500 clamp(3rem,7vw,5.6rem)/.95 Newsreader,serif;letter-spacing:-.03em}.lead{font-size:1.15rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.65}.en-page section{margin-top:2.6rem;border-top:1px solid var(--border);padding-top:1.4rem}.en-page h2{font:500 2rem/1.1 Newsreader,serif}.en-page p{line-height:1.72;color:var(--muted)}.en-page a{color:var(--brand);font-weight:700;text-decoration:none}
</style>
